```c
if (IS_GEN9_LP(dev_priv) || IS_CANNONLAKE(dev_priv)) {
    signal_levels = bxt_signal_levels(intel_dp);
}
```
Reason:
The conditional check incorrectly included only the Intel Gen9 LP and Cannon Lake generations, which caused Ice Lake (ICL) to use the wrong reference for `signal_levels`. This oversight meant that ICL was not accounted for, leading to improper voltage swing programming.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (IS_GEN9_LP(dev_priv) || INTEL_GEN(dev_priv) >= 10) {
    signal_levels = bxt_signal_levels(intel_dp);
}
```
Reason:
The patch modifies the conditional check to include all generations from Gen10 and above (which includes Ice Lake), ensuring that the correct `signal_levels` are used for ICL. This change allows the function to correctly reference the appropriate signal levels for the Ice Lake architecture, thus fixing the bug.

